Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:54:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] F635-9:
 FIX_RESET_CHARGE_DURING_PUSHBACK_WHEN_MOVEMENT_DISABLED (data 16.635.3),
 upstream ba42dfdc (#743) cherry-picked

After the visit of a pushback in flight, under the published global, a unit with a charge whose
movement is disabled (NO_MOVE / NO_MOVE_ALLOW_ATTRACT, or a row Speed >= 1 its buffs scale to 0)
loses the charge. Upstream traced it on client 16.635.1; no reference battle holds it. The 16.402
tables publish no such global and keep the old rule.

Red: the reset branch off, 3 of 22 BattleChargeTest/MovementVisitTest fail on 16.635.3; green 22/22.
Core: 16.402.22 2154/0; 16.635.3 (guard bypassed for the run) 2154/0.

(cherry picked from commit ba42dfdcf606cfafce931fdf25939a99afa5c82f)
